//! Leap-second DATE POLICY of the host adapter (Architect rulings, 3 Oct 2026; Order of 4 Oct 2026,
//! decisions C1, C7, C9 and C11). The engine (`holdover_clock_v1`) owns the safety rules and the
//! derivation of the ambiguous zone from the POSIX step mapping; this module decides what the
//! adapter stands behind and turns it into a [`LeapView`].
//!
//! Assumptions (declared, NOT proven here; all are live-qualification gates):
//! * POSIX-step semantics: the OS clock steps (chrony `leapsecmode system`); leap SMEARING sources
//!   are unsupported and excluded. An inserted second repeats a POSIX second; a deleted one skips one.
//! * The POSSIBLE-BOUNDARY SET is every month end, both kinds: ITU-R Recommendation TF.460-6 puts a
//!   leap second (+1 s or -1 s) only as the last second of a UTC month, first preference December
//!   and June, second preference March and September (general knowledge of the recommendation's
//!   text, not re-read in this repository). No transition can therefore begin inside a month; the
//!   earliest possible step at a month end `T` is `T - S` (a deletion; an insertion steps at `T`).
//! * RFC 5905 defines the NTP leap indicator as a warning of a leap second in the last minute of
//!   the CURRENT month; it states no minimum lead time, and chrony reports only Insert / Delete /
//!   Normal with no date. How early before an event any source raises the indicator is UNVERIFIED
//!   (docs/CLOCK-PROFILE-V1.md section 6: "advance leap indicator behaviour" is unverified for all
//!   four operators). One ordinary poll proves nothing about FUTURE announcement behaviour.
//! * Calendar arithmetic is civil (proleptic Gregorian, no leap seconds), on POSIX milliseconds.
//!
//! Policy:
//! * C9: a "clear" (no event pending) is never assumed across a possible boundary that no
//!   authenticated information has excluded, and no information this node can obtain excludes a
//!   FUTURE month end (no announcement lead time is qualified; the "24 h + 1 s" lead assumption of
//!   the previous policy is NOT used). So a clear ends at the earliest possible step of the first
//!   month end after the authenticated reading that established it, and an anchor is never vouched
//!   for past the earliest possible step of its OWN month end (`view`). An aged or restored claim
//!   can never extend this: the clear is recomputed from the latest authenticated reading only,
//!   and a restored record never re-establishes a clear (`restore_claim`).
//! * A poll that AUTHENTICATED reports Insert/Delete in month M names the event at the end of M,
//!   boundary `T`. The view is `Pending { kind, boundary }`; the engine expires holdover before the
//!   step instant (`T` for an insertion, `T - S` for a deletion) and refuses a sample whose interval
//!   touches the ambiguous zone `[T - S, T)` or lies past an unresolved event. NO blanket extra
//!   second is added to samples outside the zone. Pending is sticky.
//! * C1: a Pending event (and a hint) is released only by a QUALIFIED authenticated reading (NTS
//!   check passed AND uncertainty within the profile's sample ceiling) whose LOWEST possible time is
//!   at least `T + RELEASE_AFTER_BOUNDARY_MS`: an unambiguous interval wholly past the zone. The
//!   cushion is explicit OPERATIONAL POLICY (see the constant). It applies after EVERY month end,
//!   announced or not: a Normal reading whose lowest time is within the cushion after the start of
//!   its month establishes no clear (a node that missed an announcement gets the same cushion).
//! * C11: an announcement from a poll that failed the NTS check, and the leap claim of a restored
//!   record, are UNAUTHENTICATED HINTS: one slot (the earliest month end still ahead of the anchor),
//!   idempotent, applied only where it shortens the view, never on an unassessed view, never
//!   clearing or replacing an authenticated event, never evidence for a clear or a release, and
//!   never qualifying anything. Availability effect (accepted, recorded in the document): a hostile
//!   or confused source can shorten holdover by at most one step before an authenticated insertion
//!   (to the earliest possible step, which the calendar bound applies anyway without an
//!   announcement), and after a month end it names it keeps samples refused until a qualified
//!   authenticated reading past that boundary's release point releases the hint. A hint the
//!   anchor is already past is ignored.
//! * C7: `POLICY_VERSION` stays 2; a claim of any other version is discarded, so an obsolete claim
//!   gains no authority on upgrade (not even as a hint).
//! * Failed polls never extend a horizon. There is no unauthenticated fallback.
use mutiny_consensus_v8::holdover_clock_v1::{LEAP_STEP_MS, LeapClaim, LeapKind, LeapView};

/// Version of THIS date policy, stored in the leap claim of the persisted anchor (Order C7: kept at
/// 2). A stored claim of any other version is discarded. Since Order C4 and C11 a claim of THIS
/// version is at most an unauthenticated, shorten-only hint (a Pending boundary); a stored Clear is
/// never restored, so the narrower meaning of a Clear under Order C9 needs no version bump: no stored
/// claim can lengthen anything.
///
/// 2 (independent review, MINOR-1): an announcement from an unauthenticated poll is folded as the
/// kind with the earliest step and never past the current view.
pub const POLICY_VERSION: u32 = 2;
/// Order C1: an announced event (or a hint) is withdrawn only when a QUALIFIED reading's lowest
/// possible time is this far past the boundary `T`. This is explicit OPERATIONAL POLICY: it is NOT
/// derived from the timestamp mapping (labels at or after `T` are shown exactly once, so the mapping
/// alone would release at `T`) and it is NOT a measured upper bound on kernel or chrony settling
/// after the step (nothing here was measured). It reuses the defined step size `S`, so no new
/// duration is introduced; it costs at most about one second of extra abstention per event.
pub const RELEASE_AFTER_BOUNDARY_MS: u64 = LEAP_STEP_MS;

const DAY_MS: i64 = 86_400_000;

fn days_from_civil(y: i64, m: i64, d: i64) -> i64 {
    let y = if m <= 2 { y - 1 } else { y };
    let era = y.div_euclid(400);
    let yoe = y - era * 400;
    let mp = if m > 2 { m - 3 } else { m + 9 };
    let doy = (153 * mp + 2) / 5 + d - 1;
    let doe = yoe * 365 + yoe / 4 - yoe / 100 + doy;
    era * 146_097 + doe - 719_468
}
fn civil_from_days(z: i64) -> (i64, i64) {
    let z = z + 719_468;
    let era = z.div_euclid(146_097);
    let doe = z - era * 146_097;
    let yoe = (doe - doe / 1460 + doe / 36_524 - doe / 146_096) / 365;
    let y = yoe + era * 400;
    let doy = doe - (365 * yoe + yoe / 4 - yoe / 100);
    let mp = (5 * doy + 2) / 153;
    let m = if mp < 10 { mp + 3 } else { mp - 9 };
    (if m <= 2 { y + 1 } else { y }, m)
}
/// Month index `year * 12 + (month - 1)` of a POSIX millisecond instant (UTC, civil calendar).
pub fn month_index(ms: u64) -> i64 {
    let days = (ms / DAY_MS as u64) as i64;
    let (y, m) = civil_from_days(days);
    y * 12 + (m - 1)
}
/// POSIX milliseconds of 00:00:00 UTC on the first day of month `index`.
pub fn month_start_ms(index: i64) -> Option<u64> {
    let (y, m0) = (index.div_euclid(12), index.rem_euclid(12));
    let days = days_from_civil(y, m0 + 1, 1);
    u64::try_from(days.checked_mul(DAY_MS)?).ok()
}
/// Earliest nominal instant at which ANY step at the boundary `T` can begin: `T - S`, the step of a
/// deleted second (an inserted second steps at `T`). A horizon must not pass it unless an event at
/// this boundary has been excluded.
pub fn earliest_step_ms(boundary_ms: u64) -> u64 {
    LeapKind::Delete
        .step_begins_ms(boundary_ms)
        .min(LeapKind::Insert.step_begins_ms(boundary_ms))
}
/// Calendar-only horizon for an anchor adopted at `lower_ms`: holdover must expire before the
/// earliest possible step at the next month end.
pub fn calendar_horizon_ms(lower_ms: u64) -> Option<u64> {
    Some(earliest_step_ms(month_start_ms(month_index(lower_ms) + 1)?))
}
/// True when `ms` is exactly 00:00:00 UTC on the first day of a month (an event boundary).
pub fn is_month_start(ms: u64) -> bool {
    month_start_ms(month_index(ms)) == Some(ms)
}
/// The kind whose step begins earliest at the boundary `T` (a deletion steps at `T - S`, an
/// insertion at `T`): how a hint, whose kind cannot be trusted, is folded.
fn earliest_step_kind(boundary_ms: u64) -> LeapKind {
    let delete = LeapKind::Delete.step_begins_ms(boundary_ms);
    if delete <= LeapKind::Insert.step_begins_ms(boundary_ms) {
        LeapKind::Delete
    } else {
        LeapKind::Insert
    }
}
/// Order C1: a reading whose LOWEST possible time is `lo` is past the boundary `T` by the release
/// cushion.
fn past_release(boundary_ms: u64, lo: u64) -> bool {
    lo >= boundary_ms.saturating_add(RELEASE_AFTER_BOUNDARY_MS)
}

/// What one chrony poll said about the leap status, after authentication.
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum LeapObservation {
    /// No usable poll (chronyc failed, not synchronised, not authenticated): never extends.
    Unavailable,
    Normal,
    Insert,
    Delete,
}

#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
struct PendingEvent {
    kind: LeapKind,
    /// The event boundary `T`.
    boundary_ms: u64,
}
impl PendingEvent {
    fn step_begins_ms(&self) -> u64 {
        self.kind.step_begins_ms(self.boundary_ms)
    }
}

/// What the adapter currently stands behind. Lives in RAM only; a restart starts from nothing
/// except, at most, a hint from the stored claim (`restore_claim`).
#[derive(Clone, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct LeapMemory {
    /// Order C9: the earliest possible step at the first month end after the latest AUTHENTICATED
    /// Normal reading (whose interval lies in one month). It vouches for admitting a sample while no
    /// anchor exists; an anchor is bounded by its own month end instead (`view`).
    cleared_until_ms: Option<u64>,
    /// An AUTHENTICATED announcement (its kind is trusted).
    pending: Option<PendingEvent>,
    /// Order C11: the earliest month-end boundary named by an UNAUTHENTICATED hint. One slot.
    hint_ms: Option<u64>,
}

/// How a leap claim restored from the persisted anchor was treated (Order C4, C7, C11).
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum ClaimDisposition {
    /// The previous process stood behind nothing (it had not assessed the leap status).
    NoClaim,
    /// A stored announcement kept as an UNAUTHENTICATED, shorten-only hint (Order C11): the record
    /// is unkeyed, so not even a stored authenticated announcement is trusted evidence.
    Hinted,
    /// Dropped: no authority at all.
    Discarded(DiscardReason),
}
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum DiscardReason {
    /// Written by a different version of this policy (Order C7: an obsolete claim gains nothing).
    PolicyVersion,
    /// Not a value this policy can produce (a boundary that is not a month start).
    Malformed,
    /// A stored clear: a record never re-establishes or extends a clear (Order C9).
    ClearNotRestored,
}

impl LeapMemory {
    /// Fold one AUTHENTICATED poll (the host never folds an unauthenticated one here). `interval` is
    /// the UTC interval of THAT reading (wall centre +/- its own uncertainty); `None` when no reading
    /// exists. `qualified` is true when the reading also meets the profile's sample ceiling: only
    /// such a reading may release an announced event or a hint (Order C1). An authenticated reading
    /// establishes the clear of its own month whatever its width (Order C9: authenticated
    /// information, and calendar knowledge only), and an authenticated announcement is folded
    /// either way (it can only shorten).
    pub fn observe(&mut self, obs: LeapObservation, interval: Option<(u64, u64)>, qualified: bool) {
        let Some((lo, hi)) = interval else {
            return;
        };
        match obs {
            LeapObservation::Unavailable => {}
            LeapObservation::Insert | LeapObservation::Delete => {
                let kind = if obs == LeapObservation::Insert {
                    LeapKind::Insert
                } else {
                    LeapKind::Delete
                };
                let Some(boundary_ms) = month_start_ms(month_index(lo) + 1) else {
                    return;
                };
                let new = PendingEvent { kind, boundary_ms };
                self.pending = Some(match self.pending {
                    // Only a qualified reading past the old event's release point replaces it (C1);
                    // otherwise the event whose step begins earlier is kept.
                    Some(old) if !(qualified && past_release(old.boundary_ms, lo)) => {
                        if old.step_begins_ms() <= new.step_begins_ms() {
                            old
                        } else {
                            new
                        }
                    }
                    _ => new,
                });
                // Any earlier "clear" for this month end was wrong.
                self.cleared_until_ms = None;
                if qualified {
                    self.release_hint(lo);
                }
            }
            LeapObservation::Normal => {
                if let Some(p) = self.pending {
                    // C1: only a QUALIFIED reading wholly past the release point withdraws it.
                    if qualified && past_release(p.boundary_ms, lo) {
                        self.pending = None; // the event is safely past
                    } else {
                        return; // sticky: Normal cannot withdraw an unresolved announcement
                    }
                }
                if qualified {
                    self.release_hint(lo);
                }
                let month = month_index(lo);
                // C1 after EVERY month end (independent review, MINOR-2): the boundary at the start
                // of this reading's month may have carried an event this node never saw announced
                // (a blackout over the month end, or an announcement window between two polls), so
                // a reading within the release cushion after it clears nothing, exactly as if that
                // event had been announced.
                let past_month_start =
                    month_start_ms(month).is_some_and(|start| past_release(start, lo));
                if month == month_index(hi) && past_month_start {
                    // C9: the CURRENT month end only. No qualified lead time exists, so a Normal
                    // reading excludes no future boundary; a straddling reading clears nothing.
                    self.cleared_until_ms = month_start_ms(month + 1).map(earliest_step_ms);
                }
            }
        }
    }
    /// Order C1: withdraw the hint once a qualified reading's lowest time is past its release point.
    fn release_hint(&mut self, lo: u64) {
        if self.hint_ms.is_some_and(|t| past_release(t, lo)) {
            self.hint_ms = None;
        }
    }
    /// Fold an announcement from a poll that did NOT pass the NTS check as a hint (Order C11).
    /// `interval` is the UTC interval of THAT reading, as for `observe`; the hint names the month end
    /// after its lowest time (the earlier month end of a straddling reading).
    pub fn observe_unverified(&mut self, interval: (u64, u64), anchor_lower_ms: Option<u64>) {
        let Some(boundary_ms) = month_start_ms(month_index(interval.0) + 1) else {
            return;
        };
        self.hint(boundary_ms, anchor_lower_ms);
    }
    /// The one hint slot: the earliest boundary still ahead of the current anchor. Idempotent (the
    /// same hint again changes nothing) and bounded (one value, never a list).
    fn hint(&mut self, boundary_ms: u64, anchor_lower_ms: Option<u64>) {
        self.hint_ms = Some(match self.hint_ms {
            Some(old) if anchor_lower_ms.is_none_or(|a| old > a) => old.min(boundary_ms),
            _ => boundary_ms,
        });
    }
    /// Take what a restored record's leap claim may still contribute (Order C4, C7, C9, C11): a
    /// stored announcement becomes an unauthenticated, shorten-only hint; a stored clear and a
    /// claim of another policy version are discarded. Nothing is ever extended or trusted.
    pub fn restore_claim(&mut self, claim: LeapClaim) -> ClaimDisposition {
        if claim.view == LeapView::Unassessed {
            return ClaimDisposition::NoClaim;
        }
        if claim.policy != POLICY_VERSION {
            return ClaimDisposition::Discarded(DiscardReason::PolicyVersion);
        }
        match claim.view {
            LeapView::Unassessed => ClaimDisposition::NoClaim,
            LeapView::Clear { .. } => ClaimDisposition::Discarded(DiscardReason::ClearNotRestored),
            LeapView::Pending { boundary_ms, .. } => {
                if !is_month_start(boundary_ms) {
                    return ClaimDisposition::Discarded(DiscardReason::Malformed);
                }
                self.hint(boundary_ms, None);
                ClaimDisposition::Hinted
            }
        }
    }
    /// The view to push. `anchor_lower_ms` is the ADOPTED lower bound of the current anchor (not
    /// rolled). An anchor is never vouched for past the earliest possible step of its own month end
    /// unless an authenticated announcement names exactly that boundary (then its kind applies);
    /// without an anchor the latest qualified clear governs admission. A hint then shortens.
    pub fn view(&self, anchor_lower_ms: Option<u64>) -> LeapView {
        let anchor_boundary = anchor_lower_ms.and_then(|a| month_start_ms(month_index(a) + 1));
        let base = match (self.pending, anchor_boundary) {
            // An announcement for a LATER month end than the anchor's: the anchor's own month end,
            // which nothing excluded, comes first.
            (Some(p), Some(b)) if p.boundary_ms > b => LeapView::Clear {
                valid_until_ms: earliest_step_ms(b),
            },
            (Some(p), _) => LeapView::Pending {
                kind: p.kind,
                boundary_ms: p.boundary_ms,
            },
            (None, Some(b)) => LeapView::Clear {
                valid_until_ms: earliest_step_ms(b),
            },
            (None, None) => match self.cleared_until_ms {
                Some(valid_until_ms) => LeapView::Clear { valid_until_ms },
                None => LeapView::Unassessed,
            },
        };
        match self.hint_ms {
            Some(t) if base != LeapView::Unassessed && anchor_lower_ms.is_none_or(|a| t > a) => {
                let hinted = LeapView::Pending {
                    kind: earliest_step_kind(t),
                    boundary_ms: t,
                };
                if hinted.horizon_ms() < base.horizon_ms() {
                    hinted
                } else {
                    base
                }
            }
            _ => base,
        }
    }
}

#[cfg(test)]
mod tests {
    use super::*;
    use mutiny_consensus_v8::holdover_clock_v1::LeapView::{Clear, Pending, Unassessed};

    fn ms(y: i64, m: i64, d: i64, h: i64, min: i64, s: i64) -> u64 {
        ((days_from_civil(y, m, d) * 86_400 + h * 3600 + min * 60 + s) * 1000) as u64
    }
    /// The zone start a view guards (the engine's admission predicate refuses intervals reaching it).
    fn guard(v: LeapView) -> u64 {
        match v {
            Unassessed => 0,
            Clear { valid_until_ms } => valid_until_ms,
            Pending { boundary_ms, .. } => boundary_ms - LEAP_STEP_MS,
        }
    }
    const S: u64 = LEAP_STEP_MS;

    #[test]
    fn civil_calendar_matches_known_posix_instants() {
        assert_eq!(ms(1970, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0), 0);
        assert_eq!(ms(2000, 3, 1, 0, 0, 0), 951_868_800_000);
        assert_eq!(ms(2016, 12, 31, 23, 59, 59), 1_483_228_799_000);
        assert_eq!(ms(2026, 10, 1, 0, 0, 0), 1_790_812_800_000);
        assert_eq!(month_index(0), 1970 * 12);
        assert_eq!(month_index(ms(2026, 2, 28, 23, 59, 59)), 2026 * 12 + 1);
        assert_eq!(month_index(ms(2024, 2, 29, 12, 0, 0)), 2024 * 12 + 1, "leap day stays in Feb");
        assert_eq!(month_start_ms(2026 * 12 + 11), Some(ms(2026, 12, 1, 0, 0, 0)));
        assert_eq!(month_start_ms(2027 * 12), Some(ms(2027, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0)));
        // Round trip over a long range.
        for idx in (1970 * 12 + 1)..(2200 * 12) {
            let start = month_start_ms(idx).unwrap();
            assert_eq!(month_index(start), idx);
            assert_eq!(month_index(start - 1), idx - 1);
            assert!(is_month_start(start));
            assert!(!is_month_start(start + 1) && !is_month_start(start - 1));
        }
    }
    #[test]
    fn horizons_are_the_earliest_step_of_a_month_end_and_nothing_else() {
        let t = ms(2026, 12, 1, 0, 0, 0);
        // The earliest step at a boundary is the step of a deleted second, one step before it.
        assert_eq!(earliest_step_ms(t), t - S);
        assert_eq!(earliest_step_ms(t), LeapKind::Delete.step_begins_ms(t));
        assert!(LeapKind::Insert.step_begins_ms(t) > earliest_step_ms(t));
        assert_eq!(calendar_horizon_ms(ms(2026, 11, 10, 0, 0, 0)), Some(t - S));
        // The release cushion reuses the defined step; no other duration appears in this policy.
        assert_eq!(RELEASE_AFTER_BOUNDARY_MS, S);
    }

    #[test]
    fn c9_a_clear_never_crosses_a_month_end_nothing_authenticated_excluded() {
        // Order C9, over 1970..2200: a qualified authenticated Normal reading anywhere in month M
        // clears only up to the earliest possible step at the END OF M (the previous policy vouched
        // until the end of M + 1 on the unmeasured "24 h + 1 s" lead assumption). An anchor adopted
        // in M is never vouched for past that instant either, and an anchor of an EARLIER month keeps
        // its own, earlier, month end however new the reading.
        for idx in (1970 * 12)..(2200 * 12) {
            let start = month_start_ms(idx).unwrap();
            let next = month_start_ms(idx + 1).unwrap();
            let end = Clear { valid_until_ms: next - S };
            for t in [start + S, start + S + 1, next - 1] {
                let mut m = LeapMemory::default();
                m.observe(LeapObservation::Normal, Some((t, t)), true);
                assert_eq!(m.view(None), end, "month {idx}");
                assert_eq!(m.view(Some(t)), end, "month {idx}");
                assert_eq!(m.view(Some(start)), end);
                if idx > 1970 * 12 {
                    assert_eq!(m.view(Some(start - 1)), Clear { valid_until_ms: start - S });
                }
            }
            // C1 after every month end (review MINOR-2): within the cushion after the month's start
            // a Normal reading clears nothing; an anchor is still bounded by its own month end.
            for t in [start, start + 1, start + S - 1] {
                let mut m = LeapMemory::default();
                m.observe(LeapObservation::Normal, Some((t, t)), true);
                assert_eq!(m.view(None), Unassessed, "month {idx}, {} ms in", t - start);
                assert_eq!(m.view(Some(t)), end, "month {idx}");
            }
        }
    }

    #[test]
    fn c9_clear_expiry_endpoints_and_what_a_clear_needs() {
        // The horizon is EXCLUSIVE (the engine requires the rolled upper bound to stay BELOW it):
        // for a reading in November 2026, labels up to T - S - 1 are vouched for, T - S is not.
        let t = ms(2026, 12, 1, 0, 0, 0);
        let mut m = LeapMemory::default();
        m.observe(LeapObservation::Normal, Some((ms(2026, 11, 30, 23, 0, 0), ms(2026, 11, 30, 23, 0, 0))), true);
        let v = m.view(None);
        assert_eq!(v, Clear { valid_until_ms: t - S });
        assert_eq!((v.horizon_ms() - 1, v.horizon_ms()), (t - S - 1, t - S));
        // A reading whose interval straddles the month end clears nothing (the previous clear, or
        // none, stays); one that lies wholly in the next month clears the end of THAT month.
        let mut s = LeapMemory::default();
        s.observe(LeapObservation::Normal, Some((t - 13, t + 13)), true);
        assert_eq!(s.view(None), Unassessed);
        // Wholly in December but within the release cushion after its start (C1 after every month
        // end, review MINOR-2): nothing yet, down to the last millisecond of the cushion.
        s.observe(LeapObservation::Normal, Some((t, t + 26)), true);
        assert_eq!(s.view(None), Unassessed);
        s.observe(LeapObservation::Normal, Some((t + S - 1, t + S + 25)), true);
        assert_eq!(s.view(None), Unassessed);
        s.observe(LeapObservation::Normal, Some((t + S, t + S + 26)), true);
        assert_eq!(s.view(None), Clear { valid_until_ms: ms(2027, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0) - S });
        // A clear is established by an AUTHENTICATED reading (the host folds no other), whatever
        // its width, and only for its own month; an older reading's clear is never extended by time
        // passing (it is recomputed from the latest authenticated reading only).
        let mut u = LeapMemory::default();
        u.observe(LeapObservation::Normal, Some((t - 86_400_000, t - 86_400_000)), false);
        let aged = u.view(None);
        assert_eq!(aged, Clear { valid_until_ms: t - S });
        u.observe(LeapObservation::Unavailable, Some((t + 5_000, t + 5_000)), true);
        u.observe(LeapObservation::Normal, None, true);
        assert_eq!(u.view(None), aged, "a poll without a reading moves nothing");
        u.observe(LeapObservation::Normal, Some((t + 5_000, t + 5_000)), false);
        assert_eq!(u.view(None), Clear { valid_until_ms: ms(2027, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0) - S });
    }

    #[test]
    fn normal_clears_pending_announces_and_pending_is_sticky() {
        let t = ms(2026, 12, 1, 0, 0, 0); // end of November
        let mut m = LeapMemory::default();
        assert_eq!(m.view(None), Unassessed, "nothing known, no anchor");
        // Calendar-only bound for an anchor adopted mid-November.
        assert_eq!(m.view(Some(ms(2026, 11, 10, 0, 0, 0))), Clear { valid_until_ms: t - S });
        m.observe(LeapObservation::Normal, Some((ms(2026, 11, 10, 0, 0, 0), ms(2026, 11, 10, 0, 0, 1))), true);
        assert_eq!(m.view(None), Clear { valid_until_ms: t - S });
        // Insert announced in November: event at the end of November.
        m.observe(LeapObservation::Insert, Some((ms(2026, 11, 30, 12, 0, 0), ms(2026, 11, 30, 12, 0, 1))), true);
        assert_eq!(m.view(None), Pending { kind: LeapKind::Insert, boundary_ms: t });
        // The authenticated kind applies to an anchor of that month: an insertion steps at T.
        assert_eq!(m.view(Some(ms(2026, 11, 30, 12, 0, 0))), Pending { kind: LeapKind::Insert, boundary_ms: t });
        // A later Normal (flapping indicator) cannot withdraw it before the event is past.
        m.observe(LeapObservation::Normal, Some((ms(2026, 11, 30, 23, 0, 0), ms(2026, 11, 30, 23, 0, 1))), true);
        assert!(matches!(m.view(None), Pending { .. }));
        // Exact edges of the release: one millisecond short of boundary + cushion keeps it ...
        let release = t + RELEASE_AFTER_BOUNDARY_MS;
        m.observe(LeapObservation::Normal, Some((release - 1, release + 99)), true);
        assert!(matches!(m.view(None), Pending { .. }), "still inside the cushion");
        // ... a qualified reading whose LOWEST possible time is exactly boundary + cushion withdraws
        // it; Normal in December clears the end of December (C9: not further).
        m.observe(LeapObservation::Normal, Some((release, release + 100)), true);
        assert_eq!(m.view(None), Clear { valid_until_ms: ms(2027, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0) - S });
        // Delete: the clock jumps when POSIX time reaches T - 1 s.
        let mut d = LeapMemory::default();
        d.observe(LeapObservation::Delete, Some((ms(2026, 6, 30, 1, 0, 0), ms(2026, 6, 30, 1, 0, 1))), true);
        let tj = ms(2026, 7, 1, 0, 0, 0);
        assert_eq!(d.view(None), Pending { kind: LeapKind::Delete, boundary_ms: tj });
        // The engine derives the step and the zone from (kind, boundary); nothing else is stored.
        assert_eq!(LeapKind::Delete.step_begins_ms(tj), tj - S);
    }

    #[test]
    fn c1_release_requires_a_qualified_unambiguous_reading() {
        // Order C1. The cushion is policy; the release needs, on top of it, a reading that passed
        // the NTS check AND the profile's sample ceiling, whose WHOLE interval lies past T + S.
        let t = ms(2026, 12, 1, 0, 0, 0);
        let announced = || {
            let mut m = LeapMemory::default();
            m.observe(LeapObservation::Insert, Some((t - 3_600_000, t - 3_600_000)), true);
            m
        };
        let release = t + RELEASE_AFTER_BOUNDARY_MS;
        // An unqualified authenticated reading past the cushion: no release, no clear.
        let mut m = announced();
        m.observe(LeapObservation::Normal, Some((release + 5_000, release + 5_100)), false);
        assert_eq!(m.view(None), Pending { kind: LeapKind::Insert, boundary_ms: t });
        // An unqualified announcement for the NEXT month does not replace (lengthen) it either.
        m.observe(LeapObservation::Delete, Some((release + 5_000, release + 5_100)), false);
        assert_eq!(m.view(None), Pending { kind: LeapKind::Insert, boundary_ms: t });
        // A qualified reading whose LOWEST time is one ms short of T + S: not unambiguously past.
        let mut m = announced();
        m.observe(LeapObservation::Normal, Some((release - 1, release + 26)), true);
        assert!(matches!(m.view(None), Pending { .. }));
        // A qualified reading wholly past T + S releases it; so does a qualified announcement there,
        // which then names its own month end.
        let mut m = announced();
        m.observe(LeapObservation::Normal, Some((release, release + 26)), true);
        assert!(matches!(m.view(None), Clear { .. }));
        let mut m = announced();
        m.observe(LeapObservation::Delete, Some((release, release + 26)), true);
        assert_eq!(m.view(None), Pending { kind: LeapKind::Delete, boundary_ms: ms(2027, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0) });
    }

    #[test]
    fn c11_hints_are_bounded_idempotent_shorten_only_and_never_clear_or_qualify() {
        let nov_end = ms(2026, 12, 1, 0, 0, 0);
        let dec_end = ms(2027, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0);
        let mid_nov = ms(2026, 11, 10, 0, 0, 0);
        let late_nov = ms(2026, 11, 30, 12, 0, 0);
        let reading = |t: u64| (t - 13, t + 13);
        let hinted = Pending { kind: LeapKind::Delete, boundary_ms: nov_end };
        assert_eq!(earliest_step_kind(nov_end), LeapKind::Delete);
        // No view at all (no anchor, nothing authenticated): a hint has nothing to shorten.
        let mut m = LeapMemory::default();
        m.observe_unverified(reading(late_nov), None);
        assert_eq!(m.view(None), Unassessed, "a hint never assesses anything");
        // It never establishes a clear and never releases anything (an authenticated, qualified
        // reading is needed for that).
        assert_eq!(m.cleared_until_ms, None);
        // Under an authenticated Insert for the same month end, the hint shortens it to the earliest
        // step (T - S instead of T), keeps the authenticated event in place, and repeating it (any
        // number of times, from any reading in November) changes nothing.
        let mut m = LeapMemory::default();
        m.observe(LeapObservation::Insert, Some(reading(late_nov)), true);
        let before = m.clone();
        m.observe_unverified(reading(late_nov), Some(mid_nov));
        assert_eq!(m.view(Some(mid_nov)), hinted);
        assert_eq!(m.pending, before.pending, "the authenticated event is untouched");
        let once = m.clone();
        for t in [late_nov, mid_nov, late_nov + 60_000] {
            m.observe_unverified(reading(t), Some(mid_nov));
        }
        assert_eq!(m, once, "idempotent");
        // A hint for a LATER month end does not shorten a November view and is not applied; it
        // also never displaces the earlier hint (one slot, the earliest boundary).
        m.observe_unverified(reading(ms(2026, 12, 15, 0, 0, 0)), Some(mid_nov));
        assert_eq!(m.view(Some(mid_nov)), hinted);
        assert_eq!(m.hint_ms, Some(nov_end));
        // Under a clear without an anchor the hint shortens nothing that the clear did not already
        // end, and an unauthenticated Normal is not even folded (the host ignores it).
        let mut c = LeapMemory::default();
        c.observe(LeapObservation::Normal, Some(reading(mid_nov)), true);
        let cleared = c.view(None);
        c.observe_unverified(reading(late_nov), None);
        assert_eq!(c.view(None).horizon_ms(), cleared.horizon_ms());
        // A qualified authenticated reading past the hint's release point withdraws it; an
        // unqualified one does not.
        c.observe(LeapObservation::Normal, Some((nov_end + S, nov_end + S + 26)), false);
        assert_eq!(c.hint_ms, Some(nov_end));
        c.observe(LeapObservation::Normal, Some((nov_end + S, nov_end + S + 26)), true);
        assert_eq!(c.hint_ms, None);
        assert_eq!(c.view(None), Clear { valid_until_ms: dec_end - S });
        // A hint naming a month end the anchor is already past is stale for it: not applied, and
        // replaced by the next hint.
        let mut p = LeapMemory::default();
        p.observe_unverified(reading(ms(2026, 10, 20, 0, 0, 0)), None);
        assert_eq!(p.view(Some(mid_nov)), Clear { valid_until_ms: nov_end - S });
        p.observe_unverified(reading(late_nov), Some(mid_nov));
        assert_eq!(p.hint_ms, Some(nov_end));
    }

    #[test]
    fn c11_a_hint_never_lengthens_any_view_in_any_month() {
        // Every month 1970-2200, every kind of state the policy holds, hints read in that month,
        // at its end and in the next: the view's horizon and guard never move later, and an
        // unassessed view stays unassessed.
        let seeded = |obs: LeapObservation, t: u64| {
            let mut m = LeapMemory::default();
            m.observe(obs, Some((t, t)), true);
            m
        };
        let mut checked = 0u32;
        for idx in (1970 * 12 + 1)..(2200 * 12) {
            let start = month_start_ms(idx).unwrap();
            let end = month_start_ms(idx + 1).unwrap();
            let mid = start + (end - start) / 2;
            let states = [
                (LeapMemory::default(), None),
                (LeapMemory::default(), Some(mid)),
                (seeded(LeapObservation::Normal, mid), None),
                (seeded(LeapObservation::Normal, mid), Some(mid)),
                (seeded(LeapObservation::Insert, mid), Some(mid)),
                (seeded(LeapObservation::Delete, mid), Some(mid)),
                (seeded(LeapObservation::Insert, start - 1), Some(start - 1)),
            ];
            for (state, anchor) in &states {
                for t in [start, mid, end - 1, end, end + (end - start) / 2] {
                    let before = state.view(*anchor);
                    let mut folded = state.clone();
                    folded.observe_unverified((t - 13, t + 13), *anchor);
                    let after = folded.view(*anchor);
                    assert!(after.horizon_ms() <= before.horizon_ms(), "{t}: {before:?} -> {after:?}");
                    assert!(guard(after) <= guard(before), "{t}: {before:?} -> {after:?}");
                    assert_eq!(after == Unassessed, before == Unassessed);
                    checked += 1;
                }
            }
        }
        assert!(checked > 50_000, "{checked}");
    }

    #[test]
    fn review_r5_an_announcement_on_a_straddling_reading_names_the_earlier_month_end() {
        // The reviewer's missing test (mutant M16 survived at 0fb149d: the boundary inferred from
        // the reading's HIGHEST possible time). A reading whose interval straddles a month boundary
        // names the EARLIER month end (the event may be at that boundary right now), authenticated
        // or not.
        let t = ms(2027, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0);
        for (obs, kind) in [
            (LeapObservation::Insert, LeapKind::Insert),
            (LeapObservation::Delete, LeapKind::Delete),
        ] {
            let mut m = LeapMemory::default();
            m.observe(obs, Some((t - 13, t + 13)), true);
            assert_eq!(m.view(None), Pending { kind, boundary_ms: t }, "{obs:?}");
        }
        // Unauthenticated, under the calendar-only bound of a December anchor (horizon T - S): the
        // hint names T too (applied as soon as a view exists to shorten; here it equals the bound).
        let anchor = ms(2026, 12, 20, 0, 0, 0);
        let mut m = LeapMemory::default();
        m.observe_unverified((t - 13, t + 13), Some(anchor));
        assert_eq!(m.hint_ms, Some(t));
        assert_eq!(m.view(Some(anchor)).horizon_ms(), t - S);
    }

    fn claim(view: LeapView) -> LeapClaim {
        LeapClaim {
            policy: POLICY_VERSION,
            view,
        }
    }
    #[test]
    fn c4_c7_c9_c11_a_restored_claim_is_at_most_a_shorten_only_hint() {
        let nov_end = ms(2026, 12, 1, 0, 0, 0);
        let mid_nov = ms(2026, 11, 10, 0, 0, 0);
        // Nothing was assessed: nothing to restore, whatever the policy tag says.
        let mut m = LeapMemory::default();
        assert_eq!(m.restore_claim(LeapClaim { policy: 99, view: Unassessed }), ClaimDisposition::NoClaim);
        // C7: a claim of another policy version (older or newer) gains NO authority, not even as a
        // hint that could only shorten.
        for policy in [1, POLICY_VERSION + 1] {
            for view in [
                Clear { valid_until_ms: nov_end - S },
                Pending { kind: LeapKind::Delete, boundary_ms: nov_end },
            ] {
                let mut m = LeapMemory::default();
                assert_eq!(
                    m.restore_claim(LeapClaim { policy, view }),
                    ClaimDisposition::Discarded(DiscardReason::PolicyVersion)
                );
                assert_eq!(m, LeapMemory::default());
            }
        }
        // C9: a stored clear is never restored, whatever horizon it names.
        for v in [nov_end - S, ms(2027, 3, 1, 0, 0, 0) - S, u64::MAX] {
            let mut m = LeapMemory::default();
            assert_eq!(
                m.restore_claim(claim(Clear { valid_until_ms: v })),
                ClaimDisposition::Discarded(DiscardReason::ClearNotRestored)
            );
            assert_eq!(m, LeapMemory::default());
        }
        // A stored announcement that is not a month start is malformed.
        let mut m = LeapMemory::default();
        assert_eq!(
            m.restore_claim(claim(Pending { kind: LeapKind::Insert, boundary_ms: nov_end + 1 })),
            ClaimDisposition::Discarded(DiscardReason::Malformed)
        );
        // C11: a stored announcement becomes a HINT, whatever kind it names and however far away:
        // it only ever shortens (an insertion's step T becomes the earliest step T - S), it
        // establishes nothing on its own, and a far-future one has no effect until its month.
        let mut m = LeapMemory::default();
        assert_eq!(
            m.restore_claim(claim(Pending { kind: LeapKind::Insert, boundary_ms: nov_end })),
            ClaimDisposition::Hinted
        );
        assert_eq!(m.view(None), Unassessed);
        m.observe(LeapObservation::Insert, Some((mid_nov, mid_nov + 26)), true);
        assert_eq!(m.view(Some(mid_nov)), Pending { kind: LeapKind::Delete, boundary_ms: nov_end });
        let mut far = LeapMemory::default();
        assert_eq!(
            far.restore_claim(claim(Pending { kind: LeapKind::Insert, boundary_ms: ms(2030, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0) })),
            ClaimDisposition::Hinted
        );
        far.observe(LeapObservation::Normal, Some((mid_nov, mid_nov + 26)), true);
        assert_eq!(far.view(Some(mid_nov)), Clear { valid_until_ms: nov_end - S });
    }

    #[test]
    fn restoring_any_claim_never_lengthens_any_view_in_any_month() {
        // For every month and every claim shape a record can carry, the views of a memory that
        // restored the claim are never longer (horizon and guard) than those of one that did not,
        // with or without an anchor, before and after a qualified authenticated reading.
        let mut checked = 0u32;
        for idx in (1970 * 12 + 1)..(2200 * 12) {
            let start = month_start_ms(idx).unwrap();
            let end = month_start_ms(idx + 1).unwrap();
            let mid = start + (end - start) / 2;
            for view in [
                Clear { valid_until_ms: end - S },
                Clear { valid_until_ms: month_start_ms(idx + 2).unwrap() - S },
                Pending { kind: LeapKind::Insert, boundary_ms: end },
                Pending { kind: LeapKind::Insert, boundary_ms: month_start_ms(idx + 2).unwrap() },
                Pending { kind: LeapKind::Delete, boundary_ms: start },
            ] {
                let mut restored = LeapMemory::default();
                restored.restore_claim(claim(view));
                let mut plain = LeapMemory::default();
                for step in 0..2 {
                    if step == 1 {
                        restored.observe(LeapObservation::Normal, Some((mid, mid + 26)), true);
                        plain.observe(LeapObservation::Normal, Some((mid, mid + 26)), true);
                    }
                    for anchor in [None, Some(mid)] {
                        let (a, b) = (restored.view(anchor), plain.view(anchor));
                        assert!(a.horizon_ms() <= b.horizon_ms(), "{view:?}: {a:?} vs {b:?}");
                        assert!(guard(a) <= guard(b), "{view:?}: {a:?} vs {b:?}");
                        checked += 1;
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        assert!(checked > 50_000, "{checked}");
    }
